From: Brad House <bhouse@nexthop.ai>
Subject: zebra: install remote EVPN-MH MACs as static fdb entries

Kernels with the fix for CVE-2026-98023 ("vxlan: reject dynamic fdb
entries that reference a nexthop id") refuse to add or update a dynamic
fdb entry that uses an nhid:

  zebra: Extended Error: A nexthop fdb cannot be dynamic
  zebra: netlink-dp (NS 0) error: Invalid argument, type=RTM_NEWNEIGH(28)

zebra installs remote MACs behind an Ethernet Segment exactly that way
(NUD_REACHABLE + NTF_EXT_LEARNED + nhid), so none of them is programmed
and traffic to them floods to every VTEP of the ES, which can duplicate
it. zebra owns these entries (install, move, delete); the kernel should
never age them. Set NUD_NOARP when a remote MAC references a nexthop
group. Kernel readback of vxlan fdb entries does not look at NUD_NOARP,
so this changes only what is installed.

Interim local patch; to be replaced by the upstream FRR fix.

Forwarded: not-yet
Last-Update: 2026-11-15
---
diff --git a/zebra/rt_netlink.c b/zebra/rt_netlink.c
index e883033..e5380c8 100644
--- a/zebra/rt_netlink.c
+++ b/zebra/rt_netlink.c
@@ -3728,6 +3728,15 @@ ssize_t netlink_macfdb_update_ctx(struct zebra_dplane_ctx *ctx, void *data,
 	}
 
 	nhg_id = dplane_ctx_mac_get_nhg_id(ctx);
+
+	/* The kernel rejects dynamic fdb entries that reference a nexthop
+	 * ("A nexthop fdb cannot be dynamic", CVE-2026-98023). Remote MACs
+	 * behind an ES are owned by zebra and must not be aged by the
+	 * kernel anyway, so install them as static.
+	 */
+	if ((update_flags & DPLANE_MAC_REMOTE) && nhg_id)
+		state |= NUD_NOARP;
+
 	vtep_ip.ipaddr_v4 = *(dplane_ctx_mac_get_vtep_ip(ctx));
 	SET_IPADDR_V4(&vtep_ip);
 
